{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-history screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant’s criminal record before making a conditional offer, and after a conditional offer may consider only the convictions the act lists, after an individualized assessment.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; does not include a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Rental dwelling unit means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; inquiries about methamphetamine-related convictions on federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registration are permitted.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 (no prior violation), $5,000 (one prior violation) or $10,000 (two or more); director may order compliance actions and payment to the applicant up to $1,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors. The director may order the application fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; does not include a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Duty attaches before the housing provider accepts any application fee.","coverage_quotes":["Rental dwelling unit means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant’s rental application fee be returned; monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 apply to violations.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after overturned director order","requirement":"If a court overturns, on the provider’s successful appeal, a director’s order requiring the provider to rent to an applicant, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant, who must receive at least 45 days’ notice.","key_value":"45 days’ notice","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units owned by the housing provider and occupied by a former applicant as the result of a director’s order; excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Only where a provider’s successful appeal overturns a director’s order to rent to the former applicant.","coverage_quotes":["Rental dwelling unit means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

